  "notice": "2026-08-03: SPEC.md v1.0 section 7 rule 5 kept crystallisation additives that sat within 5.0 A of the peptide and merely flagged them.  That rule was a SPEC DEFECT, not a pipeline bug - corpus_build.py implemented it exactly as written.  A glycerol, PEG, sulfate or acetate packed against the peptide is a crystallisation artefact; in solution that space is water, so keeping it means docking into a pocket partly filled by something that was never biologically there, and lets the additive be scored as part of the receptor.  complex.cif is now strict; the previous file is complex_permissive.cif and nothing was deleted.  See SPEC.md section 14.",
